"distance":0.3763,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3951,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3976,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"WAS","distance":0.4463,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"CAR","distance":0.4545,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Joe Brady"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"CAR","distance":0.8162,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"CLE","distance":1.052,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"TB","distance":1.104,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Todd Bowles"},{"season":2018,"team":"BUF","distance":1.104,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"CAR","distance":1.123,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals went 3-13 in 2018 and were outscored 425 to 225. The defense did most of the work, finishing 20th in EPA allowed while the offense ranked 32nd in EPA per play. What set them apart was the highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense struggled, ranking 25th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. They were one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Josh Rosen ran the passing game, with Larry Fitzgerald leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Cardinals defense was a little below average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the pass than the run, ranking 7th and 31st. Chandler Jones led the team with 13 sacks, and Rodney Gunter added 4.5 despite playing only 58% of the snaps. Schematically, they had the highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Cardinals were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 71% of field goals, which was one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 8% of the money on the books.","players":"Josh Rosen played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 2,278 yards. Larry Fitzgerald was the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 734 receiving yards. David Johnson handled most of the work in the backfield with 78% of the carries. On defense, Chandler Jones led the team with 13 sacks and Tre Boston picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2020 Broncos and the 2022 Steelers. Their defense looked most like the 2022 Panthers and the 2019 Browns.","trends":"2018 is the first season covered here, so there is no earlier year to compare it with. The charts below show how the Cardinals changed over the seasons that followed.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2018. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}